From e76e655c048a26e138269e0636f9da75dc2c01eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:25:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: wireless: qcom,ath12k: add qcom,no-sbs

The firmware of the dual-MAC chips can run its two radios in the two halves
of the 5 GHz band at the same time (single band simultaneous). Some boards
have no 5 GHz path on the second radio; describe that so that the driver
can tell the firmware.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath12k.yaml      | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath12k.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath12k.yaml
index 27947f1d64..37c431772c 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath12k.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath12k.yaml
@@ -28,6 +28,13 @@ properties:
       If present, a board or platform specific string used to lookup
       usecase-specific firmware files for the device.
 
+  qcom,no-sbs:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The board cannot run the two radios of the chip in the two halves of
+      the 5 GHz band at the same time (single band simultaneous, SBS): the
+      second radio has no 5 GHz path. The firmware must be told not to use it.
+
   vddaon-supply:
     description: VDD_AON supply regulator handle
 
-- 
